dehe deha-bhṛtāṁ vara\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2379,\"bb\":2111,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/4/b2111/\",\"shadow_value\":\"adhibhūtam – the physical manifestation; kṣaraḥ – constantly changing; bhāvaḥ – nature; puruṣaḥ – the universal form, including all the demigods, like the sun and moon; ca – and; adhidaivatam – called adhidaiva; adhiyajñaḥ – the Supersoul; aham – I (Kṛṣṇa); eva – certainly; atra – in this; dehe – body; deha-bhṛtām – of the embodied; vara – O best.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"adhibhūtam\",\"translation\":\"the physical manifestation\"},{\"word\":\"kṣaraḥ\",\"translation\":\"constantly changing\"},{\"word\":\"bhāvaḥ\",\"translation\":\"nature\"},{\"word\":\"puruṣaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the universal form, including all the demigods, like the sun and moon\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"adhidaivatam\",\"translation\":\"called adhidaiva\"},{\"word\":\"adhiyajñaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the Supersoul\"},{\"word\":\"aham\",\"translation\":\"I (Kṛṣṇa)\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"atra\",\"translation\":\"in this\"},{\"word\":\"dehe\",\"translation\":\"body\"},{\"word\":\"deha-bhṛtām\",\"translation\":\"of the embodied\"},{\"word\":\"vara\",\"translation\":\"O best\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2380,\"bb\":2112,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/4/b2112/\",\"body_value\":\"O best of the embodied beings, the physical nature, which is constantly changing, is called adhibhūta [the material manifestation]. The universal form of the Lord, which includes all the demigods, like those of the sun and moon, is called adhidaiva. And I, the Supreme Lord, represented as the Supersoul in the heart of every embodied being, am called adhiyajña [the Lord of sacrifice].\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2381,\"bb\":2113,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/4/b2113/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 8.4\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 8.4\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Library\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"}],\" » \"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/bg/8/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"hre